    "body": "2026 SEMA Show • Hybrid Honda Passport Throws More HP in Baja Racing Than Any Other 9.0-Liter V8-Powered Trophy Truck\nVolkswagen Commercial Vehicles Relaunches the Caravelle Nameplate In the UK, Starting From £41,960*\n6 photos\nPhoto: Volkswagen Commercial Vehicles\nVolkswagen Commercial Vehicles may be dedicated solely to VW AG’s light commercial vehicles, but it’s entirely committed to its job, like all professionals are. So, it’s no wonder that they often have more news up and coming than some larger mainstream brands.\nJust recently, they said they were busy making various announcements in the United Kingdom: VCV has been named the ‘Most Reliable Vanmaker’ for the third consecutive year by the UK’s fleet companies in the Fleet News FN50 annual rankings, but they also have product novelties.\nIn addition to the showcase of the flexible autonomous ID. Buzz platform at NVIDIA GTC Berlin, back in October Volkswagen Commercial Vehicles kicked off the preparations for the 2027 camping season with the Grand California campervan getting updates for MY27, like a new interior and optional solar panels, while a Dune Special Edition was also added to the UK lineup.\nThat’s not all, because just a few days ago the UK order books were opened for the facelifted California campervan , with first deliveries expected in early 2027 and prices kicking off at £54,065 or $73k, with the refreshed models featuring an improved front-end design, updated cockpit, and the latest comfort and safety technologies, with added benefits like the 5+ Promise, Volkswagen’s enhanced warranty and service plan.\nAnyway, they are not slowing down, and now Volkswagen Commercial Vehicles is replacing the outgoing Multivan moniker with a fresher premium seven-seat people carrier as the brand reintroduces the Caravelle nameplate to the UK. Available to order starting November 5, 2026, it is priced from £41,960 or about $53,539 at the current exchange rate.\nHowever, there’s a caveat: just like in the case of the refreshed California campervan, the new Caravelle is priced without VAT, so you're going to have to pay more if you can't deduct the tax in the UK . Anyway, the new seven-seat people carrier can also be had from £499 per month on a Solutions Personal Contract Plan, with first customer deliveries expected in early 2027.\nIt has a new exterior and interior style, the latest technology, seven seats as standard, as well as an optional six-seat configuration. It will be available with the regular Life and Style trims but also with a new Edition grade starting from £49,960 (excl. VAT), which is over $63k. There are features like the new VW Bus headlights, a new-generation ‘free-standing’ 12.9-inch infotainment system, as well as an upgraded 10.25-inch Digital Cockpit.\nThere are two solid colors, eight metallic paints, and even three dual-tone finishes (Candy White/Starlight Blue metallic, Candy White/Grey Brown Metallic, Grenadilla Black Metallic/Sunset Red Metallic), plus a Black Roof option exclusively for the Edition trim.\nThe latter brings a dark-tinted two-piece panoramic sunroof, glossy black 18-inch Brussel alloy wheels, and dark LED rear lights, plus dark silver brushed inserts; a dark headliner and door pillar trim; and ergoComfort seats in dark ArtVelours microfleece upholstery for the interior.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nVolkswagen Caravelle Volkswagen Multivan Volkswagen Caravelle minivan volkswagen commercial vehicles pricing UK\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT Trio of New Morbidelli T802 Motorcycles Will Make Short Work of Every Surface",
